From 8de5ed4263e6f1af2677e4e6a511d50a90dd8398 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Rebe?= <rene@exactco.de>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:55:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mesa: map user-array bits before masking them with the draw's
 arrays
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

_mesa_get_derived_vao_masks() combined the unmapped VAO masks with the
mapped @enabled_attribs before it applied the POS/GENERIC0 attribute
mapping.  Take a compatibility-profile fixed-function draw whose
position comes from glVertexAttribPointer(0, ...) in client memory
(ATTRIBUTE_MAP_MODE_GENERIC0).  The mapped mask has POS set and the
unmapped user mask has GENERIC0 set, so the intersection lost the
array and the mapping step had nothing to move.  The state tracker
then took the "no user buffers" fast path and dereferenced the NULL
BufferObj of that binding in st_update_array_templ().

Classify user and non-zero-divisor arrays in the VAO's own attribute
space, apply the mapping, then restrict the result to the enabled
arrays.

Reproduced on the Parhelia driver with an 8-line program
(glVertexAttribPointer(0/1) user arrays, no program bound,
glDrawElements); before this change it segfaulted, now it draws.  This
also fixes piglit depth-tex-modes-glsl when its program does not link
and the test falls back to fixed function.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
---
 src/mesa/main/arrayobj.h | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/arrayobj.h b/src/mesa/main/arrayobj.h
index 279d7ec..21ad5f3 100644
--- a/src/mesa/main/arrayobj.h
+++ b/src/mesa/main/arrayobj.h
@@ -173,8 +173,11 @@ _mesa_get_derived_vao_masks(const struct gl_context *ctx,
    const GLbitfield enabled_nonuser = enabled & vao->VertexAttribBufferMask;
    const GLbitfield enabled_nonzero_divisor = enabled & vao->NonZeroDivisorMask;
 
-   *enabled_user_attribs = ~enabled_nonuser & enabled_attribs;
-   *nonzero_divisor_attribs = enabled_nonzero_divisor & enabled_attribs;
+   /* Classify in the VAO's own attribute space, map, then restrict to what
+    * the draw enables: masking with the mapped @enabled_attribs first drops
+    * a user array that the mapping moves between POS and GENERIC0. */
+   *enabled_user_attribs = ~enabled_nonuser & enabled;
+   *nonzero_divisor_attribs = enabled_nonzero_divisor;
 
    switch (vao->_AttributeMapMode) {
    case ATTRIBUTE_MAP_MODE_POSITION:
@@ -199,6 +202,8 @@ _mesa_get_derived_vao_masks(const struct gl_context *ctx,
    default:
       break;
    }
+   *enabled_user_attribs &= enabled_attribs;
+   *nonzero_divisor_attribs &= enabled_attribs;
 }
 
 
